From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: winex11: a minimized Linux program's window keeps its size

David (2026-11-15): "open OBS, minimize it and unminimize it, and only one of
the 4 categories will show, like just Sources." A Linux program's window in
its Wine frame (0762, sg_embed.c) is sized to the frame's client area; a
minimized frame has none, so the program was made 1x1 (max(1, 0)), and Qt
laid OBS's docks out for that and kept it when restored. Minimized, the
program is still told so (WM_STATE Iconic, _NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN) but keeps
its size; restored, the frame's client area is what it was.

Gate: test/linuxembed-gate.sh: the framed program's window is not resized
while its frame is minimized (mutant SG_MUTANT_EMBED_MINIMIZED_RESIZED).
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -743,6 +743,17 @@
         X11DRV_check_error();
     }
 #endif
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_MINIMIZED_RESIZED
+    if ((style & WS_MINIMIZE) && find_hwnd( data->hwnd ))
+    {
+        /* minimized, the frame has no client area: the program keeps its
+         * size (made 1x1, Qt laid out OBS's docks for that and kept it when
+         * restored: one of Sources, Scenes, Controls left -- David
+         * 2026-11-15) */
+        pthread_mutex_unlock( &embed_mutex );
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     if ((e = find_hwnd( data->hwnd )))
     {
         /* its shadow outside the frame (clipped by it) */
